// ── TRACK 3 · LAYER 2 · MOTION ────────────────────────────────────────────
// The hook. 16ths, but the cell is a WAVE, not a ladder: root → 5th → 3rd →
// colour tone. A straight ascending arp reads as an exercise; the up-then-down
// contour reads as a melody that happens to be fast.
//
// The 4th note of every cell is chosen to land a step or a third from the next
// cell's first note (…b4→a4 at the loop seam is a step), so 8 bars of 16ths
// still trace one continuous line.
//
// Colour tones: added 9ths on Am/G/C, and Bm7 in bar 5. F# is in the D and Bm
// cells — that is the Dorian 6th doing the lifting up here where it's audible.
// Delay is a dotted 8th (0.375s at cps 0.5) with high feedback: the echoes
// land between the 16ths and fill the space the original track packed with
// notes. Space instead of density is the whole brief for this track.
// HARMONY FIX: this used `<...>*4`. On a slowcat, *n means n ITEMS PER
// CYCLE, so the whole 8-chord progression raced past 4x while the bass
// made one pass — verified from the events sidecar: the bass changed chord
// every cycle while this layer played the entire scale in every cycle. It
// sounded merely blurry rather than wrong only because everything is
// diatonic. The multiplier now lives INSIDE each cell, so the note count and
// rhythm are unchanged but each chord is locked to its own bar.
setcps(0.5)
stack(
  note(`<[[a4 e5 c5 b4]*4]
         [[g4 d5 b4 a4]*4]
         [[c5 g5 e5 d5]*4]
         [[d5 a5 f#5 e5]*4]
         [[b4 f#5 d5 a4]*4]
         [[c5 g5 e5 d5]*4]
         [[d5 a5 f#5 e5]*4]
         [[a4 e5 c5 b4]*4]>`)
    .s("square")
    .lpf(sine.range(900, 3600).slow(8)).lpq(8)   // one full sweep per loop
    .gain(0.17).release(0.05)
    .delay(0.36).delaytime(0.375).delayfeedback(0.38)
    .pan(0.44).room(0.18).size(0.7)
)
